5) main decisions implemented (BR21/BR22/BR23 on top of the preserved B01-B04 lineage)
   BR21: ONE constant-size last-consumed-now high-water scalar on ControlMailbox (property
        last_consumed_now_ns); every consume with structurally valid nonnegative now/slot and a valid
        caller age cap rejects now < last accepted clock (equality allowed) and records the new now
        BEFORE the pending candidate is inspected, so empty, evicted, aged-out, missed-slot and
        future-completion paths all establish the observed clock; malformed arguments change no state;
        a regressed clock raises BrokerError and preserves pending candidate, high-water key/digest and
        history; no internal clock reads, no per-call history list, no implicit reset (new binding =
        new mailbox); a future completion is retried at equal/later clock only.
   BR22: the frozen profile age cap is a hard bound for consumption; age_limit_ns must satisfy
        0 < age_limit_ns <= PROFILE_LIMITS[binding.profile].observation_age_limit_ns (fast_9600 1.5 s,
        stress_300 12 s); an excessive value raises BrokerError even on an empty mailbox and before any
        clock state is recorded; effective expiry is now >= sample_lower + age_limit; no silent widening.
   BR23: non-stop LeaseDeadline audit terms are mode-scoped: HIL mandatory first_send_plus_original_ttl
        and sample_lower_plus_age_limit (optional receipt_plus_remaining_budget, previous_deadline);
        PC_DIRECT mandatory first_host_issue_plus_requested_duration and sample_lower_plus_age_limit
        (optional previous_deadline only); unknown, missing, cross-mode and duplicate names and invalid
        ints raise BrokerError; deadline = min(terms) unchanged and revalidated on every expired_at;
        stop state stays deadline None / empty terms / nonempty reason; the docstrings state that a
        matching audit structure is not cryptographic provenance and never movement authorization.
   preserved lineage (semantically unchanged from recovery2): persisted high-water key/digest/
        completion metadata independent of the pending candidate; fail-closed clock consistency at
        offer and consume (sample lower, future completion retained for retry); mandatory immutable
        uint64 sent_ordinal with <=4 retained observations, idempotent exact duplicates, no
        re-registration of evicted ordinals, no wrap/restart in a binding; PROFILE_LIMITS read-only;
        BrokerBinding frozen profile names; sample_lower <= first_send/first_host_issue guards;
        unknown receipt bounds still stop.
   fail-closed convention (documented in the module and consume docstrings): clock-inconsistent
        inputs raise BrokerError; scheduling outcomes without a usable result return no candidate.

